    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. so if you had to categorize it, would you say we're seeing a fundamental decline in the quality of contemporary art because of this? like, is the move away from formal beauty actually making the work less \"good\" in a professional sense, or is it just a different kind of value?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I wouldn't say that the quality of contemporary art is necessarily declining, but rather, the definition of quality is evolving. The shift away from formal beauty and towards conceptual or conceptual-art-like works can lead to a different kind of art being recognized as \"valuable\" or \"good.\" This new paradigm prioritizes the idea and message conveyed over traditional notions of artistic skill or aesthetics. It's a different kind of value, but one that is widely recognized in contemporary art circles.",
      "source": "target",
